    "media:imagetext": "AP\nFor Your Safety\n737-800\nOver Water\nIf you are sitting in an exit row please identify yourself to a crew\nmember to allow for reseating if: You lack the ability to read, speak,\nor understand the language, or the graphic form, or the ability to\nunderstand hand signals and oral crew commands in English.\nPor Su Seguridad\nSi usted esta sentado en una fila junto a una salida favor de\nidentificarse a un asistente de vuelo para que podamos asignarle\notro asiento si: usted falta abilidad a leer, hablar, o comprender el\nidioma, or forma grafica or abilidad a comprender senales de\nmano y instrucciones verbales de la tripulacion en Ingles.\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push, pull, and maneuver when\nopening. Because of this, and for the safety of all passengers, Federal Law requires\nthat we only seat qualified passengers next to exits. If you are sitting in an exit row,\nyou may be asked to open the exit and assist our crew in the event of an\nemergency. Please ask to be reseated if you:\n• Lack the strength, mobility, or dexterity in your arms, hands, and legs required:\n- To reach upwards, sideways, and downwards to the location of emergency exit\nand exit-slide operating mechanisms;\n- To grasp and push, pull, turn, or otherwise manipulate those mechanisms;\n- To push, shove, pull, or otherwise open emergency exits;\n- To lift out, hold, deposit on nearby seats, or maneuver over the seatbacks to\nthe next row objects the size and weight of over-wing window exit doors;\n- To remove obstructions similar in size and weight to over-wing exit doors;\n- To reach the emergency exit expeditiously;\n- To maintain balance while removing obstructions;\n- To exit expeditiously;\n- To stabilize an escape slide after deployment; or\n- To assist others in getting off an escape slide;\n• Are less than 15 years old or lack the ability to perform the listed duties without\nassistance from an adult companion, parent, or other relative.\n• Lack sufficient visual capacity to perform one or more of the applicable duties\nwithout the assistance of visual aids beyond contact lenses or eyeglasses.\n• Lack sufficient aural capacity to hear and understand instructions by the crew,\nwithout assistance beyond a hearing aid\n• Lack ability to give oral commands to others.\n• Have a physical condition that may not be visible but may prevent you from\nassisting in the above activities.\n• Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to care for) which would\nprevent you from assisting.\n• Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit would injure you.\n• Do not wish to help in this way.\nFederal regulations require all passengers, regardless of where they are sitting or\ntheir physical condition, to review this card, for their safety.\nFederal regulations require customer compliance with lighted information signs,\nposted placards, areas designated as non-smoking, and crew member instructions\nwith regard to these items.\nWhen finished reviewing this card, please return it to the seat pocket for our next customer.\nPM0474 (Orig. 7/04)",
